From 4bda5d4d3ea901250d0364af5b8fc43738334f35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bubunuh <76405364+bubunuh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:35:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/21] DeathInference: a ghoul rallied to the trees is no
 unlisted phantom

A ghoul trained from a crypt rallied onto the trees walks off to work on its
own and may never be selected; the lists never naming it is no sign that the
order was refused. Units WC3V saw sent to harvest (harvestConfident) are no
longer counted as never made.

Dev games: Undead army value error 70 -> 62, all 78 -> 76.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/DeathInference.js | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/DeathInference.js b/lib/DeathInference.js
index 434d950..3059db1 100644
--- a/lib/DeathInference.js
+++ b/lib/DeathInference.js
@@ -253,7 +253,10 @@ class DeathInference {
     // 3b. A trained unit the player's selection lists never show, long after
     //     it was due: most likely an order the game refused (no gold, no food)
     //     or a cancelled one. Whatever path it has belongs to another unit.
+    //     Not a ghoul its building's rally sent to the trees: it goes to work
+    //     without ever being selected.
     if (unit.selectionUnlisted && !isWorker && unit.trainedTime != null &&
+        !unit.harvestConfident &&
         gameEnd - unit.trainedTime >= LOST_MS) {
       return {
         state: 'possiblyLost',
-- 
